Feature: TC_16_STAFF - OpenShift Migration Search, Maps and Navigation E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for Openshift Cases" (BISSAGL-12669, AT-TC-01 to 10)
  # Rewritten 16-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario on the OpenShift deployment; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   After the move to OpenShift the main staff journeys still work: side menu, Home searches by reference, herd and
  #   parcel, map generation by parcel and by herd (with download details and paging), Online Response, an internal
  #   amendment, every side menu area of an application, and the Active Farmer admin check entry point.
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - Legacy only searched in AT-TC-02 to 04 and 07; the searches here run the same way.
  #   - AT-TC-08 had a branch that deleted every admin inspection when "Admin Inspection is Completed." was already on
  #     screen before Amend was clicked. That destructive branch is not carried over; the amendment is submitted
  #     without scheme changes and confirmed.
  #   - AT-TC-10 stopped after Start admin check; Section 10 checks that Send is offered and does not send, so no
  #     payment stop is applied to the herd.
  #   - Each user switch signs out first, as legacy started each scenario with a fresh login.
  #
  # Test data:
  #   Herds, reference numbers and LPIS parcels from the database ("Get Submitted Herds", "Get Reference Numbers",
  #   "Get LPIS Parcels"), as in legacy.
  #   Logins agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1), agr11612 and agr2332 (map printing users, as in legacy).
  #   Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case, the same for all three.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  @regression @staff @openshift @search @maps @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-OS-MIGRATION-E2E-01 - Staff runs the main BISS journeys on the OpenShift deployment

    # SECTION 1 : Switch between side menu areas - AT-TC-01
    Given the staff user is logged in to the OpenShift BISS portal as "agr4442"
    When the staff user navigates the dashboard side menu
      | Coordination |
      | Home         |
    Then the dashboard should remain available

    # SECTION 2 : Search with a reference number - AT-TC-02
    When the staff user searches the Home screen for the next reference number for scheme year "2023"

    # SECTION 3 : Search with a herd number - AT-TC-03
    When the staff user searches the Home screen for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2024"

    # SECTION 4 : Parcel search - AT-TC-04
    When the staff user searches the Parcels screen for the next LPIS parcel for scheme year "2024"

    # SECTION 5 : Generate a map from a parcel search - AT-TC-05
    When the staff user signs out of the portal
    Given the staff user is logged in to the OpenShift BISS portal as "agr11612"
    And the staff user is on the Map Printing screen
    And the staff user is searching by parcel
    When the staff user searches Map Printing for the next LPIS parcel for scheme year "2023"
    And the staff user requests a map with the following settings
      | parcels | single               |
      | mapType | Inspection Discovery |
      | legend  | yes                  |
    Then the map generation request should be accepted

    # SECTION 6 : Generate a map from a herd search, check its details, page the maps table - AT-TC-06
    When the staff user signs out of the portal
    Given the staff user is logged in to the OpenShift BISS portal as "agr2332"
    And the staff user is on the Map Printing screen
    When the staff user searches Map Printing for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2023"
    Then the staff user should see the herd identity details
      | name    |
      | address |
    When the staff user requests a map with the following settings
      | parcels | single              |
      | mapType | Full Color Ortho A4 |
      | legend  | yes                 |
    Then the generated map should be recorded with the following details
      | status     |
      | id         |
      | herdNumber |
      | date       |
    And the generated map should reach its final status
    When the staff user pages through the generated maps table
      | Next page     |
      | Previous page |
    Then the generated maps table should remain displayed

    # SECTION 7 : Online Response search - AT-TC-07
    When the staff user signs out of the portal
    Given the staff user is logged in to the OpenShift BISS portal as "agr4442"
    When the staff user searches the Online Response screen for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2023"

    # SECTION 8 : Internal amendment without scheme changes - AT-TC-08
    When the staff user amends the application for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user submits the amendment and confirms

    # SECTION 9 : Every side menu area of an application - AT-TC-09
    When the staff user opens the application for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2024"
    Then the following application tabs should be available
      | Payments         |
      | Correspondence   |
      | Errors/Stops     |
      | Inspections      |
      | Notes/History    |
      | BISS Application |
      | SIM              |

    # SECTION 10 : Active Farmer - the admin check can be started - AT-TC-10
    When the staff user opens the application for the next submitted herd for scheme year "2023"
    And the staff user opens the "Active Farmer" screen
    Then the start admin check confirmation should be offered
